entity provision_block {
  name     = "provision {} block"
  kind     = :wcl_block
  summary  = "Names a wscript file that runs on `vmlab up`, declared inside the vm/container it configures."
  related  = [provisions, on_handler, wscript_overview, labs, playbook_block]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "A `provision {}` block runs a wscript file on `vmlab up`. It is declared **inside** the `vm {}` or `container {}` it belongs to — that machine is its target, so there is nothing to name. It runs once, after that machine is ready, at its position among the machine's steps."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
vm "dc01" {
  template = "x86_64/windows-server-2025"

  provision "scripts/setup.ws" { }              // 1st, once dc01 is ready
  playbook  "playbooks/domain" { play = "dc" }  // 2nd
  provision "scripts/verify.ws" { }             // 3rd, sees the converged guest
}
SRC
    }
    p "**Provision failures fail `vmlab up`.** A machine's steps gate `depends_on`: anything depending on `dc01` starts only after dc01's provisions and playbooks have finished. Inside the script, `lab.this_vm()` returns the owning machine — VM or container alike — while `lab.machine(\"name\")` reaches any other — a script that stands up a DC and then joins a member is still one script, declared on whichever machine should gate it. The same block inside a `template {}` runs on the build VM."
  }
}
